From: wnduddld0513 <wnduddld0513@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sensor: report a missing sensor as an initialization error

When SUID discovery finds no sensor for the requested data type, the async
initialization returned FALSE without a GError. GAsyncInitable callers then
receive NULL with *error unset, and the TB520FU IMU bridge dereferenced the
NULL error while the SSC was still registering sensors at boot (SIGSEGV).
Return SSC_SENSOR_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE instead.

---
diff --git a/src/libssc-sensor.c b/src/libssc-sensor.c
--- a/src/libssc-sensor.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor.c
@@ -522,7 +522,9 @@
 			g_signal_handler_disconnect (self, priv->report_id);
 			priv->report_id = 0;
 
-			g_task_return_boolean (ctx->task, FALSE);
+			/* Initialization failed: callers read the error message */
+			g_task_return_new_error (ctx->task, ssc_sensor_error_quark (), SSC_SENSOR_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE,
+						 "No '%s' sensor available", priv->data_type);
 			g_clear_object (&ctx->task);
 			g_slice_free (ReportReceivedContext, ctx);
 
